<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gilmar Pisas</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gilmar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pisa">Pisas</a> is a Curaçao politician who has been prime minister of Curaçao, a country within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Kingdom of the Netherlands</a>, since 2021. He leads the Movement for the Future of Curaçao party and previously headed an interim government in 2017.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gilmar-pisas.jpg" alt="Gilmar Pisas" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ministerie van Buitenlandse Zaken · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gilmar_Pisas,_2022.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
